  "name": "Nanai and Ulch song and shamanic music (Lower Amur)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Nanai and Ulch, Tungusic fishing peoples of the lower Amur in Khabarovsk Krai. Shamanic rites are led by a shaman chanting invocations to a single-headed frame drum, represented here by a generic frame-drum card, and the clanging iron cones of the shaman's belt, while secular songs are sung solo and the one-string ducheke fiddle is played. The repertoire is preserved in the Pushkin House phonogram archive and Amur field recordings.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1940s nanai and ulch song and shamanic music, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. credited frame drums, ducheke. field recording. small-diaphragm pencil condenser, portable field-recorder pre. tape 15ips.",
